 **Description:** Running Exp 4296 either writes `blocked_arc_fixtures_missing` when the offline solver import, survey, Exp 4285 progress artifact, Exp 4275 progress artifact, Exp 4261 wall artifact, Exp 4244 routing artifact, or local fixture metadata cannot support the attempt, writes `complete: incremental_progress_no_advance_<game>_L<n>_<reason>` when the selected non-`ls20` non-`wa30` non-`sc25` game has no verifier-routed real-env level increment in this bounded run, or writes `success: incremental_progress_<game>_advanced_to_L<n>_total22` only when the offline real environment confirms one new level after the hardened set-encoder route is accepted. A successful run MUST set `total_levels=22`, `levels_completed=1`, `game_advanced` to the non-`ls20` non-`wa30` non-`sc25` advanced game id, `real_env_confirmed=true`, `verifier_validated=true`, preserve model specs for the offline world-model solver and hardened set-encoder routing, report the selected game/level and why it was selected, and compute `reproducibility_checksum` from deterministic solver inputs and trajectory evidence. An honest no-advance run MUST keep `total_levels=21`, set `levels_completed=0`, set `game_advanced="none"`, set `real_env_confirmed=false`, keep the selected non-`ls20` non-`wa30` non-`sc25` `target_game` and `target_level` attributable, and still satisfy the acceptance gate when `honest_verdict` is terminal-prefixed with `complete:`. A blocked run MUST keep `total_levels=21`, set `levels_completed=0`, set `game_advanced="none"`, and still satisfy the acceptance gate because the verdict is terminal-prefixed with `blocked_`.
+
